","10–15+ Years","Process/Production Manager","15+ Years","Plant Manager / Head of Manufacturing"]},{"type":"h","text":"Best overall positioning"},{"type":"p","text":"For B.Tech/B.E. Textile Engineering / Technology → Process Engineer, the strongest profile is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Textile Manufacturing","Process Engineering","Quality Control","Lean/Six Sigma","Automation","Data Analytics","Sustainable Manufacturing"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The student should gain hands-on factory exposure during the degree because process engineering in textiles is highly dependent on understanding real machines, process parameters, production constraints and quality defects—not just theoretical textile knowledge."},{"type":"table","header":["237","UG","Engineering & Technology","B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Textile Engineering / Technology","Textile Designer",""],"rows":[]}]}]}